     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Hi Rui,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Thanks for your interest in BioGeoBEARS! I&#39;ve added you.</span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Re: colors, you can see how the default colors are generated here:</span></font></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px;font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#legends\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts%23legends&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484668501000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1geXPcsFNN1xhQ8qSUdvIA\">http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#legends</a></span><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Once you&#39;ve used this to make &quot;colors_list_for_states&quot;, then just add &quot;colors_list_for_states= colors_list_for_states&quot; into the arguments for plot_BioGeoBEARS_results(), wherever it appears in your script.</span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">As you can see in the first script, &quot;mix_colors_for_states&quot; is what mixes the single-area colors into the mixed colors for the (many, many) ranges with multiple areas.</span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Or, you could just manually specify &quot;</span></font><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">colors_list_for_states&quot; as a list of colors, but if you have 350 possible states/ranges, you will have to specify 350 colors.s</span></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Cheers!</span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Nick</span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"># States</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">res2 = plot_BioGeoBEARS_results(results_object, analysis_titletxt, addl_params=list(&quot;j&quot;), plotwhat=&quot;text&quot;, label.offset=0.45, tipcex=0.7, statecex=0.7, splitcex=0.6, titlecex=0.8, plotsplits=TRUE, cornercoords_loc=scriptdir, include_null_range=TRUE, tr=tr, tipranges=tipranges)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"># Pie chart</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">plot_BioGeoBEARS_results(results_object, analysis_titletxt, addl_params=list(&quot;j&quot;), plotwhat=&quot;pie&quot;, label.offset=0.45, tipcex=0.7, statecex=0.7, splitcex=0.6, titlecex=0.8, plotsplits=TRUE, cornercoords_loc=scriptdir, include_null_range=TRUE, tr=tr, tipranges=tipranges)</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div></font></div><span style=